course: dictionary
lesson: 6354
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. The word mower has two meanings: a machine that cuts grass, and a person who cuts grass or hay. «Dad pushed the mower across the lawn.» You push a machine, so here a mower is the machine.
explain: Read the words around it. «The farm hired two mowers to cut the hay before the rain came.» Hired means people were paid for a job, and hay is grass for animals, so here a mower is a person. Ask yourself: does this fit a machine, or a person?
explain: Mowers come in different kinds. A push mower is pushed by hand, and a ride-on mower is one you sit on. Mower is a noun, so you can have one mower or many mowers.
explain: The blades of a mower are sharp and fast, so keep away while it runs. «A lawnmower blade can spin about fifty times a second and can throw stones, so children stay indoors or far away while it runs.»
fact: Mower is a noun. You can say a mower or mowers.
fact: A mower is a machine for cutting grass, also called a lawnmower.
fact: A mower can also be a person who cuts grass or hay.
fact: «Lawn mower», «push mower» and «ride-on mower» are all ways of naming the machine.
fact: Never put your hands or feet near a mower's blades, and stay well away while it runs.
exercise: «Dad pushed the mower across the lawn.» What is a mower here? | *A machine for cutting grass | A kind of bird | A large brown bag | A person who sells flowers
exercise: «The farm hired two mowers to cut the hay before the rain came.» What is a mower here? | A tall tree | A kind of seed | A cup of tea | *A person who cuts grass or hay
exercise: Why should children stay far away from a mower that is running? | *Its sharp, fast blades can throw stones | It cannot hear children | It likes to be left alone | It needs quiet to work
test: «He sat on the ride-on mower and cut the front lawn.» What is the ride-on mower? | A type of chair | *A machine for cutting grass | A person who cuts hay | A horse
test: Which phrase means the same as lawnmower? | Rake | *Lawn mower | Garden hose | Hedge trimmer
exam: Read this: «The mower stopped, and the mower went home for lunch.» What does the second mower mean? | A kind of hat | *A person who cuts grass or hay | A machine for cutting grass | A garden shed
